From 1d6f52c1a8f41ce7e9a6eb3640d7233c2bb25cd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:31:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 06/14] fix(tekton,kubevirt): refuse wrongly typed params and
 networks arguments

The server registers tools through the go-sdk raw AddTool path, which
does not validate arguments against the input schema, so each handler
checks its own. Three handlers dropped a wrongly typed value instead:

- tekton_task_start and tekton_pipeline_start read `params` with a type
  assertion to an object; a string (for example "greeting=hello") was
  ignored and the run started without parameters, with a success answer.
- vm_create read `networks` with a type assertion to an array; a string
  was ignored and the VM was created without its secondary networks.

These arguments are now refused with an error that names the expected
type, before anything is read or written. A missing or null argument
behaves as before. The broader issue, schema validation of tool
arguments, is the same root cause as #1584 and is not changed here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
